  "version": 192,
  "released": "2026-08-22",
  "changelog": "v192: docs: the child-interaction paradigm, Play, the three loops, and the Studio vocabulary, written down once each. interactions/README.md gains § \"The child-interaction paradigm\": Conversation is the parent, each child adds exactly ONE goal (placement v188 / onboarding v189 / identity v190; arc walking is PROPOSED, platform issue #570), a stage-keyed prompt/turn-instructions.md leaf the host substitutes into, ONE additive structured-output field gated on a TurnShape flag, and its own lints + goldens + evals harness — plus a table of the four children with field names, stages, stage sources, closed validators, and lint counts, and the stated training path (train the small interactions first, one model later). Play semantics are stated once, everywhere: Play APPROVES the row and STARTS its conversation, with the approving write (promote / scaffold / graduate) running in the host's background job — \"Play is read-only\" / \"Play never promotes\" is retired vocabulary (platform ADR 0020 amended ADRs 0018/0021/0022 in place). Each child README now carries a Platform-twin table naming exactly what a host reads (question_candidate gained one). The glossary and the README's Nomenclature gain Play, Play target (proposed), child interaction, placement aside, onboarding context, identity context, episode/plan (proposed), Current (the version you'd hand someone today — the CLI's `final` star), Foundation / Review / Queue, the three loops, and Question queue. README.md and docs/handbook/the-loop.md now state the Loop as two users of one system (a passive user answers one quick daily question and over time gets a full life story; an active user answers more, holds longer conversations, and looks at how their life is being built), name the three loops with their entrypoints and real step order transcribed from the shell scripts, and document the weekly queue as an AGGREGATION WITH A FORMULA (question_planner.build_queue: dynamic Focus weighting, group caps main 0.50 / project 0.35 / focus 0.25, least-covered category first, objective boost ×2.5, chapter-gap fraction 0.15, story-function caps, rumination cooldown ×0.25, the escalation gate, arc_max 2) with file:line citations and three new handbook parity annotations. CLAUDE.md and AGENTS.md gain operating notes for the next agent: the four children, the additive-field discipline and the TurnShape stand-in landmine a host hits on every pin bump, and \"a message points at a place; a printer prints a command\" (v191's format_chapter_offer split). Docs only — no behavior change, no prompt or eval file touched.",
